{
  "about": "tools/check/round-checks.py's mapping from changed paths to the focused checks that cover them. `prefixes`: a changed file under `path` selects these lit paths (relative to ctcompile/test; a trailing / means a directory), CTests (exact names), build targets and commands. The longest matching prefix wins, so a shared helper can be given a narrow entry under a broad one. A changed lit test or test helper under ctcompile/test with no entry selects itself (a test file) or its directory (a helper). `always` is added whenever anything is selected. `heavy` tests are left out of every selection (a negative lookahead in the filter) unless a changed file starts with one of their `when` prefixes; then they run with their `lit_flags`. Edit freely; round-checks.py --self-test does not read this file.",
  "always": {
    "lit": [
      "CTNative/Lowering/Objects/",
      "CTNative/Lowering/Closures/",
      "CTNative/Optimization/",
      "CTNative/Fixtures/"
    ],
    "targets": [
      "ctjs-opt",
      "ctjs-translate",
      "ctcompile-tool",
      "ctcompile-test-native-reference",
      "ctcompile-fixture-inputs"
    ],
    "commands": [
      "python3 tools/check/check-workload.py fixture"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "CTNative/Fixtures reads build-time pipeline modules: build ctcompile-fixture-inputs, or the Fixtures tests fail on stale inputs (ctcompile/test/README.md)."
    ]
  },
